WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:11.480
Today we're going to talk about the Democratic People's Republic of Korea: the only country

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:16.850
in the world named quite-so ironically. You
may know it better as North Korea. It's

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.850
as democratic as a country ruled by the same
family for 70 years can be!

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.840
The head of state has been inherited through three generations of Kim's family:

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:32.460
Kim Il-Sung, Kim Jong-Il, and now Kim Jong-Un. And in keeping with this perfectly democratic

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.770
tradition, the leader of North Korea is called, not president, not king, but 'Supreme Leader'.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.519
You know, just like any normal democracy.

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:49.539
So, what can we really say about North Korea
that you haven't heard before? Well, it is

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:53.979
one of the most brutal dictatorships in the
whole world, where mass torture, execution,

00:00:53.979 --> 00:00:56.539
and extreme poverty are common.

00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:59.879
And now you might ask, 'Why should we care so much about this country?'

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:05.500
Well, the answer is as simple as, 'NUCLEAR BOMBS!' This is a country that is still

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.291
officially at war with South Korea and makes a pastime of threatening Japan and the US

00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:15.000
with nuclear annihilation. And while that
might have sounded far-fetched at one time,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.920
with nuclear tests happening almost every
other year, people are starting to take Lil'

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.930
Kim seriously.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:31.560
But you might still wonder... if North Korea is that dangerous, well, why isn't anyone

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.560
stopping them?

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.970
So, they've actually tried. Basically every
sanction you could think of has been thrown

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:42.550
at North Korea. But instead of that financial pressure forcing reform, North Korea has just

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:47.390
had it's diplomats selling meth out of their
embassies worldwide. Two shockers there: One,

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:53.770
yes indeed, there are North Korean embassies.
And two, yes, they also sell drugs out of

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.770
them.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:02:00.790
But there's one country that still calls
North Korea a friend - and that's China!

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.860
They even have a treaty called the 'Sino-North
Korean Mutual Aid and Cooperation Friendship

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.690
Treaty'.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:13.150
'China and Korea are as close from each
other as lips are close to teeth' --Mao

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.150
Zedong

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.819
China, and to a lesser extent Russia, have
been the only things propping up the North

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:23.000
Korean regime. So, that gives China a lot
of sway over Kim Jong-Un, right? Well, that's

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.639
what the international community thought...
And that's how China came to be seen as

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:32.120
the only country the world could turn to in
order to rein in North Korea's nuclear ambitions.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:38.239
But not so fast. Things are changing. And
China is starting to get rather annoyed at

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:42.450
their little brother's tomfoolery.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:47.379
So the question today is what's behind the
cooling of the relationship between China

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:52.510
and North Korea? And what consequences could
this have on the future of the country? Joining

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.830
us today to answer these questions is the
biggest China expert on YouTube. Yes, dear

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:00.870
viewers, we are talking about Chris Chappell,
the host of CHINA UNCENSORED.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.040
Hello Simon and hello to all our friends at
VisualPolitik.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.919
So relations between these two communist brothers
have deteriorated so much that China and North

00:03:08.919 --> 00:03:12.670
Korea are in the middle of a war... of words!

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:19.430
Basically, China said that it would work with
the evil imperialists'you know, the USA to

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.780
combat North Korea's nuclear program.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.139
Then North Korean state-run media responded that China should really think about how its

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:30.709
'reckless act of chopping down the pillar
of [North Korea]-China relations' could

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.410
have 'grave consequences.'

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:38.239
And then Chinese state-run media responded with a not so subtle threat to end their alliance.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:41.709
So why exactly are they stabbing each other in back? Well, we're going to have a look

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:45.450
at that right now!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.609
CHINA FRIENDZONES NORTH KOREA

00:03:47.609 --> 00:03:52.501
China and North Korea really make the perfect
best friends. They have much in common: They

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:57.499
share a border, they both had communist uprisings,
and have installed leaders who have radical

00:03:57.499 --> 00:04:01.959
views of Marxism. The People's Republic
of China and the Democratic People's Republic

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:12.409
of Korea really are like the Quentin Tarantino
and Robert Rodriguez of the international

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:13.590
politics!

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:18.470
'Now China does more than just give North Korea financial aid. China has also made big

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.770
loans to the North Korean regime so they can
build railroads and highways. And they're

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:25.730
pretty forgiving when Pyongyang can't pay
back its debts.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:32.250
And then there's oil. For decades, China
was the main source of dinosaur juice to North

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.250
Korea.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:40.850
Plus, there's military cooperation. China
helped train North Korean hackers... hackers

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:46.060
who've now become a threat to the international community, including China.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:52.010
And what does Beijing get in exchange? Well,
North Korea is a cheap labor paradise. In

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:58.420
fact, many products with the 'MADE IN CHINA' label should acutally say: 'MADE IN DPRK'.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:04.260
'Australian sportswear brand Rip Curl made a public apology this week after it emerged

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:11.280
that some of its ski gear had been made in
one of North Korea's state-owned factories'

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.870
But hold on a minute, because things are starting to change. The Chinese Communist Party today

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:21.170
is a little less interested in the global
spread of Communism, and a little more interested

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:27.540
becoming a global superpower. And North Korea is, well, really cramping its style.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.480
Imagine how hard it is to be cool with America when your good buddy North Korea keeps threatening

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:37.470
to bomb them. But this is not the end of the story. 60 years ago, North Korea and China

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:46.770
were pretty similar. But today, things are
quite different...

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:55.690
A lot of  North Korean citizens would do whatever it

00:05:55.690 --> 00:06:00.370
takes in order to cross the Chinese border. And Beijing is scared of what could become

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.250
a refugee crisis similar to that of Syria.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.680
If this wasn't enough, Pyongyang's
diplomacy hasn't been all that diplomatic

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:15.510
